    {
      "id": "claim_8f77894e700646f9b8b41de03afa4743",
      "statement": "DirectoryService.build_trust_block embeds the L3 signals in every v1 profile and search result as trust.vouches_in (the same active inbound edges as the graph endpoint, listed per-edge with scope, timestamps, and voucher_tenure_hours — never collapsed into a count or score) and trust.vouch_annotations, with honest empty defaults when the VouchService is unwired; reputation_history is currently hard-coded to [] so past vouch revocations are not yet folded into it, and search's optional min_vouches_in=N filter gates inclusion on len(trust[\"vouches_in\"]) — counting visible active edges, explicitly not quality — while the legacy /agents/{fp} and /search aliases drop the trust block entirely.",
      "evidence": [
